  "creator": "jaguirresza",
  "title": "Voyager-Aligned Layout (macOS)",
  "notes": "Go60 layout aligned with my ZSA Voyager layout (Oryx R7Y9a).\n\n- Base: Voyager alpha block on rows 2-4 (` / Tab / Shift on the left edge, \\ / ' / Shift on the right). Number row = Magic 1-0 Backspace. Bottom row: Tab Ctrl Opt | Opt Ctrl Delete.\n- Shift: double-tap either Shift for Caps Word.\n- Thumbs (tap / hold): left Space/Raise, Backspace/Lower; right Esc/Lower, Enter/Raise. Outer thumb key on each side (next to the bottom row) is Cmd.\n- Lower (1): numbers and symbols, F1-F12 on the top row.\n- Raise (2): arrows on the HJKL row, Opt+arrows above, Cmd+arrows below; undo / cut / copy / paste under Z X C V.\n- Mouse (5): turns on automatically while the right trackpad moves (off after 500 ms). J K L = left / middle / right click, comma = Mission Control, period = Spotlight.\n- Magic (3) and Factory (4): unchanged from the Go60 factory layout.",
  "tags": [
    "qwerty",
    "mac",
    "voyager"
  ],
  "custom_defined_behaviors": "behaviors {\n    td_lshft_cw: td_lshft_cw {\n        compatible = \"zmk,behavior-tap-dance\";\n        #binding-cells = <0>;\n        tapping-term-ms = <200>;\n        bindings = <&kp LSHFT>, <&caps_word>;\n    };\n    td_rshft_cw: td_rshft_cw {\n        compatible = \"zmk,behavior-tap-dance\";\n        #binding-cells = <0>;\n        tapping-term-ms = <200>;\n        bindings = <&kp RSHFT>, <&caps_word>;\n    };\n};",
